# Spring Boot (`microservices/`)

Architecture: **Domain-Driven Design + Hexagonal** (ports and adapters), applied pragmatically.

## Base package

Service root: `com.github.miguelsombrero.osaan.<service_snake_case>` (matches the service folder and Maven artifact).

Typical layers under that root:

- `api/` — REST controllers, request/response DTOs (records), API mappers
- `application/` — port interfaces, application services
- `domain/` — entities, value objects, domain repository interfaces
- `infrastructure/` — driven adapters (`persistence/`, `cache/`, `client/`, `config/`, mappers, etc.); extra subpackages are normal — follow the existing service
- `config/`, `exception/`, `util/` when present

## Conventions

- Constructor injection only — Lombok `@RequiredArgsConstructor`, `private final` fields
- One class per file; package segments lowercase singular nouns where applicable
- Business logic lives in the domain layer; not in controllers or infrastructure adapters
- Do not use `var`; use explicit types
